# Agenda de aulas

Alunos marcam aulas e o professor confirma.

Stack: Flutter.

## Run it locally

### Prerequisites

- Flutter SDK
- Git
- Android Studio (or Xcode, on a Mac)

### Step by step

1. Clone the repository and enter the folder:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/you/agenda-de-aulas.git
   cd agenda-de-aulas
   ```
2. Install the dependencies:
   ```bash
   flutter pub get
   ```
3. Copy the variables and fill in the values:
   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```
4. Run the app on an emulator or a connected phone:
   ```bash
   flutter run
   ```

### Environment variables

| Variable | What it is for | Where to get it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `API_URL` | API address, passed with --dart-define. Ships inside the app: anyone can read it. | Example: `https://api.exemplo.com` |

No secret value is kept in the repository: fill in secrets only in your .env.

## Folder structure

| Folder | What it holds |
| --- | --- |
| `lib/main.dart` | App entry point. |
| `lib/features/` | One folder per feature, with screens and logic. |
| `lib/data/` | API and local database access. |
| `test/` | Tests. |
| `pubspec.yaml` | Dependencies, icons and fonts. |

